        <mxCell id="c145" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the three threshold cells, each with its name written beside it as a label (in the workbook the name shows in the Name Box, here that of B6); every later formula reads the name, not the cell. In blue: the expectation at the 2025 rate, the recorded returns, the difference (39,002.09, 19.1% of the expectation) and its percentage. In coral: the two comparisons and the conclusion, which says to investigate because the difference is above the clearly trivial threshold and below performance materiality. Column A is narrower than the workbook&#x27;s, so a long label is cut where its neighbor&#x27;s value begins.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="697" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
